{"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"amountRatio"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"amountRatio","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot14GPUParticles2DC11amountRatioSdvp","symbolKind":"property"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GPUParticles2D"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"final"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"amountRatio"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"set"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducing the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GPUParticles2D\/amountRatio"},{"type":"text","text":" has no performance benefit, since resources need to be allocated and processed for the total "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GPUParticles2D\/amount"},{"type":"text","text":" of particles regardless of the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GPUParticles2D\/amountRatio"},{"type":"text","text":". If you don’t intend to change the number of particles emitted while the particles are emitting, make sure "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GPUParticles2D\/amountRatio"},{"type":"text","text":" is set to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":" and change "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GPUParticles2D\/amount","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to your liking instead.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Note","style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/gpuparticles2d\/amountratio"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The ratio of particles that should actually be emitted. If set to a value lower than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.0"},{"type":"text","text":", this will set the amount of emitted particles throughout the lifetime to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"amount * amount_ratio"},{"type":"text","text":". Unlike changing "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GPUParticles2D\/amount","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", changing "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GPUParticles2D\/amountRatio","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" while emitting does not affect already-emitted particles and doesn’t cause the particle system to restart. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GPUParticles2D\/amountRatio","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" can be used to create effects that make the number of emitted particles vary over time."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GPUParticles2D\/amountRatio"},"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/GPUParticles2D/amount":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/gpuparticles2d\/amount","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The number of particles to emit in one emission cycle